1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:01,865
Whoever comes in eats.

2
00:00:01,989 --> 00:00:03,162
But you work.

3
00:00:03,591 --> 00:00:06,376
Xu Yan, you're mad!

4
00:00:06,637 --> 00:00:08,509
They'll eat all the grain,

5
00:00:08,686 --> 00:00:11,110
and you're the ones who starve!

6
00:00:11,179 --> 00:00:12,876
The grain lasts two months.

7
00:00:12,944 --> 00:00:14,727
Two months, one canal.

8
00:00:15,060 --> 00:00:16,943
One hoe, one bowl.

9
00:00:21,969 --> 00:00:23,225
A foot deeper!

10
00:00:23,288 --> 00:00:24,750
Ten feet dug, one bowl.

11
00:00:24,813 --> 00:00:26,107
Names, tell her.

12
00:00:26,325 --> 00:00:26,957
Next!

13
00:00:29,925 --> 00:00:30,936
New shoes.

14
00:00:31,904 --> 00:00:33,429
Calloused hands.

15
00:00:33,789 --> 00:00:34,761
They're asking—

16
00:00:35,056 --> 00:00:37,502
where the silent woman lives.

17
00:00:37,745 --> 00:00:38,477
Watch them.

18
00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:39,400
Keep it quiet.

19
00:00:39,459 --> 00:00:41,484
Not one peck sold?

20
00:00:41,547 --> 00:00:42,536
One night,

21
00:00:42,607 --> 00:00:44,535
and it's down by half!

22
00:00:44,614 --> 00:00:46,345
Xu Yan—!

23
00:00:47,186 --> 00:00:47,957
The register?

24
00:00:48,016 --> 00:00:49,806
It's for tomorrow's rations.

25
00:00:51,437 --> 00:00:52,321
This writing…

26
00:00:52,655 --> 00:00:54,594
Neat as a palace document.

27
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:55,447
Just writing.

28
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:56,849
Nice hand.

29
00:00:56,910 --> 00:00:57,764
No questions.

30
00:00:57,820 --> 00:01:00,654
Work for food: done.

31
00:01:02,937 --> 00:01:03,591
Three.

32
00:01:04,165 --> 00:01:04,891
Drums?

33
00:01:05,365 --> 00:01:06,278
The hill.

34
00:01:08,965 --> 00:01:09,569
Bandits.

35
00:01:10,165 --> 00:01:10,879
Men,

36
00:01:11,055 --> 00:01:12,532
a few dozen.

37
00:01:12,594 --> 00:01:14,237
Hundreds of torches…

38
00:01:14,321 --> 00:01:15,224
Shut the gate.
